### Fix Approaches
- IdentifiedIssue: The custom URL parsing logic for host extraction is vulnerable to an open redirect. It incorrectly truncates the host at the first colon (port separator) even if additional domain labels follow, leading to `https://example.com:8080.evil.com` being validated as `example.com`.
- Example Code in the world: A robust URL parsing library would correctly extract the full host component (e.g., `example.com:8080.evil.com`) for validation, preventing truncation.
- FixApproach: The fix ensures that the `extracted_host` always captures the entire host component of the URL, including any port or subsequent domain labels, up to the path/query/fragment separators. This prevents premature truncation at a port, ensuring the full host is used for domain validation.
